Business processes are typically managed through established guidelines, 
and process monitoring helps organizations identify deviations from these 
standards. Process mining tools facilitate the analysis of real processes 
within companies, enabling the detection of non-compliant activities. 
However, these tools currently only offer descriptive insights into process 
infractions. To address this limitation, a new approach is proposed that 
enables the development of predictive models for process monitoring. This 
approach is demonstrated through a case study, and the challenges involved 
in creating a prescriptive process monitoring framework are discussed. 
Furthermore, potential research avenues are outlined to advance the field. 
The proposed framework is made available as an open-source tool. 
Additionally, a publicly accessible dataset is provided to support future 
research. 
